    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Certificate Pinning and What It Costs',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains certificate Pinning, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] Pinning a server's public key stops interception by a certificate authority the device trusts but the app's author did not expect, and it also locks every app out the day the server changes keys unless backup pins, a sensible choice of key and a way to update were planned; that cost is why browsers dropped server-set pins. [[slnc 600]] Think of it this way. [[slnc 300]] Instead of letting any notary in the country vouch for your bank, you carry a photo of the one banker you know. A forger with a perfectly genuine notary stamp is turned away. But if the bank changes its banker, everyone who carries the old photo walks away from the real bank too, until they get a new photo. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is a mobile banking app. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will be able to: [[slnc 300]] Explain what a pin adds to certificate validation and what it does not replace. [[slnc 300]] Choose between pinning a leaf, an issuing C A and a backup key. [[slnc 300]] Describe the rotation outage and how to plan for it."),
